      <div type="clause" n="41">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 41</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXVII. Se mon se ðe bocland<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.6"/> hæbbe, ⁊ him his mægas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.7"/> læfden, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> setton we, þæt he hit ne moste sellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.8"/> of his mægburge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.9"/>, gif þær bið gewrit oððe gewitnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.10"/>, ðæt hit ðara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.11"/> manna forbod wære þe hit on fruman gestríndon ⁊ þara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.11"/> þe hit him sealdon, þæt he swa ne mote; ⁊ þæt þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> on cyninges ⁊ on biscopes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.12"/> gewitnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.10"/> gerecce beforan his mægum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="74" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXVII. Se mon se þe b..d hæbbe, ⁊ him his mægas l..., gif ...witnes...þara manna... wære ...fruman ..yndon ⁊ þara þ ... seald ..,. swa ne mote; ⁊ ..onne on cy.. ⁊ on bisceop.. gewitnesse ..ce beforan his magum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="74" ed="#liebermann"/>XXXVII. Se mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.5"/> se þe boclond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.9-2"/> hæbbe, ⁊ him (þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.7-2"/>) his yldran læfdon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.7-2"/>, þonne setton we, ðæt he hit ne mot syllan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.1"/> of his mægburge, gif ðær bið gewrit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.10-2"/> oððe gewitnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.11-2"/>, ðæt hit ðara monna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.5"/> forbod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.12-2"/> wære ðe hit on fruman gestrindon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.13-2"/> ⁊ ðara ðe hit him sealdon, ðæt he swa ne mote; ⁊ þæt þonne on cyninges ge on biscopes gewitnesse gerecce beforan his magum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="75" ed="#liebermann"/>Be boclande<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.2"/> … … … .</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="75" ed="#liebermann"/>De eo qui terram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.3"/> testamentalem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.4"/>(hereditariam) habet, quam ei parentes sui dimiserunt, ponimus, ne illam extra cognationem suam mittere possit, si scriptum intersit testamenti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.5-2"/> et testes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.6-2"/>, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.7-3"/> eorum prohibitio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.8-2"/> fuerit qui hanc inprimis adquisierunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.9-3"/> et ipsorum qui dederunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.10-3"/> ei, ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_41.lnote.oe.11-3"/> hoc possit; et hoc in regis et episcopi testimonio recitetur coram parentela sua.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="82" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be boclande…<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Af_41.attnote.fn.9"/>.] Se mon se ðe bocland hæbbe, ⁊ him his mægas læfden<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Af_41.attnote.fn.10"/>, þonne setton we, þæt he hit ne moste<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_41.attnote.fn.11"/> sellan of his mægburge, gif þær bið gewrit oððe gewitnes<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Af_41.attnote.fn.12"/>, ðæt hit ðara manna forbod<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Af_41.attnote.fn.13"/> wære þe hit on fruman gestríndon ⁊ þara þe hit him sealdon, þæt he swa ne mote; ⁊ þæt þonne on cyninges ⁊<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_41.attnote.fn.14"/> on biscopes gewitnesse gerecce beforan his mægum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="43" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="340" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXXVII} Se mon se ðe bocland hæbbe, ⁊ him his mægas læfden, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> setton we, þæt he hit ne moste sellan of his mægburge, gif þær bið gewrit oððe gewitnes, ðæt hit ðara manna forbod wære þe hit on fruman gestríndon ⁊ þara þe hit him sealdon, þæt he swa ne mote; ⁊ ðæt þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> on cyninges ⁊ on biscopes gewitnesse gerecce beforan his mægum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="75" ed="#liebermann"/>Jemand, der Urkunden-Grundbesitz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.1"/> hat, welchen ihm seine Verwandten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.2"/> hinterliessen: [über ihn] setzten wir nun fest, dass er ihn nicht aus seiner Sippe veräussern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.3"/> darf, wenn Urkunde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.4"/> oder Zeugniss vorhanden ist, dass dies ein Verbot sei [von Seiten] jener Personen, die ihn zu Anfang erwarben, und jener, die ihn ihm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.5"/> gaben, dass er so nicht [veräussern] dürfe; und dies erweise [wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.6"/> die Veräusserung anficht] mit des Königs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.7"/> und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_41.lnote.de.8"/> des Bischofs Zeugniss vor seinen Verwandten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Someone who holds land by charter, which his kinsmen left him: [concerning him] we have now determined that he may not alienate it from his kindred, if there is a document or witness that this was a prohibition [on the part] of those persons who acquired it in the beginning and of those who gave it to him, that he might not [alienate it] so; and let [whoever challenges the alienation] prove this with the witness of the king and of the bishop before his kinsmen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="83" ed="#attenborough"/>We have further established, that a man who holds land by title-deed<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_41.attnote.n.1"/>, which his kinsmen have left him, shall not be allowed to give it out of his kindred, if there is documentary or [other] evidence that the power to do so is forbidden him by the men who first acquired it, or by those who gave it to him. [And he who contests such an alienation] shall make a declaration to this effect in the presence of his kindred, with the king and bishop as witnesses.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="415" ed="#whitelock"/>The man who holds bookland, which his kinsmen left to him—then we establish that he may not alienate it from his kindred if there is a document or witness [to show] that he was prohibited from doing so by those men who acquired it in the beginning and by those who gave it to him; and that is then to be declared<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_41.whinote.n.1"/> in the witness of the king and of the bishop, in the presence of his kinsmen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="341" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>[In the case of] the man who has bookland which his kin left to him: we thus determine that he may not sell it out of his kindred if there is writing or testimony that it was forbidden by those who first acquired it or by those who gave it to him, that he thus might not [remove it from the family possession]. And let him [who is contesting the sale] declare this in the presence of his kin with the knowledge of the king and of the bishop.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="290"><label>explained by</label> <ref target="clause:IEw_2">I Ew 2</ref> <quote>One of Alfred's most important laws was about 'bookland', and it helps to explain what his son said about it (n. 124: Af 41)</quote></note>
